data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, each element is 8 bytes. The native-sized integer types (`nint`/`nuint`, introduced in C# 9) are valid `stackalloc` targets just like any other unmanaged type.
